JAX can only differentiate functions as they are defined. jax.numpy.sign(0) is 0 by definition, a convention adopted from numpy.sign. When you pass that function through autodiff, JAX will differentiate it according to its definition. If you want to differentiate a version of sign that uses a different convention, you'll have to define that function with the behavior you have in mind.
