    def eager(x):
        assert False, "Hello world"

    return better_pure_callback(eager, jax.ShapeDtypeStruct((), x.dtype), x)

f(jax.numpy.asarray(1))

FWIW I'd suggest only using the above in tests, and not as part of any public API. If you're going to wrap jax.jit for public use then there are other changes I'd still recommend making here -- for example preserving the pytree-ness of f.

