conversation.output:
@rgommers , your example does not have a problem. This issue is about the following example
@jax.jit
def func(x1):
    x2 = jnp.ones((3, 2), device=x1.device)
where x1.device is not defined inside the definition of jitted function.
Within a jitted function, "create a new array of ones with given shape on the same device as that of the input array" is pointless in the sense that the opposite "create a new array of ones with given shape on the another device as that of the input array" is not supported (it would require graph break support that would trigger device memory management tasks outside of the kernel execution).

