conversation.output:
Python does not allow overloading logical operators. The implementation of and in the interpreter always calls bool on the left operand. This is easier to see if we desugar f1 and f2:
@jax.jit
def f1(x, a, b):
    return jax.lax.cond(bool(a < x) and x <= b, 
                        lambda _: 666, 
                        lambda _: 999, 
                        None)

@jax.jit
def f2(x, a, b):
    return jax.lax.cond(bool(x > a) and (x <= b), 
                        lambda _: 666, 
                        lambda _: 999, 
                        None)
This is not allowed at tracing time, because tracing uses abstract values which have no reasonable bool interpretation.

