This computest the same result with a single dispatch event, and will therefore be much more efficient:
def f(x):
  return jnp.sin(x)
y = jax.vmap(f)(x)
If you write JAX code that looks like the former (i.e. for loops over data), it will be slow. If you write code that looks like the latter, it will be fast.

