Hi - thanks for the request! I can't see any way that we'd be able to make this work: bar(b, c) is a Python function call that is evaluated, and the result is then passed to vmap. Because of this, there's no way for vmap to interact with the values of b and c that you are passing to bar.
of course, you could pass b and c via an outer function that's wrapped in vmap in order for vmap to know about them; something like this:
@vmap
def outer(a, b, c):
  return bar(b, c)(a)
But this is basically re-constructing vmap(f).

